{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"soapstone-tin-gander","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nFP verification over all 348 historical G7 findings: at priority >= 0.85, 0 clearly-incorrect findings (22 CORRECT / 7 UNCLEAR across >= 0.75), with direct evidence authors revised plans in the demanded direction within minutes. The 0.80-0.85 band is empty (priorities quantize), so 0.85 selects the same historical set as 0.80 with less future exposure. Two noise shapes need fixing first: an unresolvable parent is emitted as a finding instead of an abstain (18f9), and same-issue duplicates stack (76d2 carried 3 findings for one issue). Only 3 findings carry plan-v4 kind grades yet, so the calibration must be rechecked once ~20 accumulate.\n\n## Approach\n(1) criteria_routing.json: G7 blocking_enabled true at 0.85 restricted to findings graded contradicts_reality (omits_required_site and incomplete_enumeration stay advisory/coached). (2) Rubric fixes in plan_review_G7.md: an unresolvable parent produces an abstain-with-coverage note, never a finding; a CLOSED parent's contract is checked against its final state, and scope the parent explicitly handed to siblings is not a leaf violation; same-issue findings must be folded into one (one finding per contradicted parent clause). (3) Pass-3 dedup: collapse multiple G7 blocking findings citing the same parent clause before the verdict. (4) Record a follow-up check in the description of this ticket's close notes: re-run the FP classification once >= 20 kind-graded G7 findings exist. Alternative rejected: enabling at 0.80 — admits future validity-0.8 findings with no historical quality evidence.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json, src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_G7.md, src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py (same-clause dedup), tests/llm/test_g7_blocking.py, docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md (regenerated).\n\n## Testing\nUnit: a contradicts_reality-graded G7 finding at 0.88 blocks; an omits_required_site finding at 0.95 stays advisory; two findings citing the same parent clause collapse to one before decide; rubric text asserts the abstain and closed-parent rules.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] contradicts_reality G7 findings at >= 0.85 block; other kinds never block (checked: decide unit tests).\n- [ ] Same-parent-clause G7 findings dedup to one before the verdict (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] The rubric contains the abstain-on-unresolvable-parent and closed-parent rules (checked: rubric text test).\n- [ ] The criteria guide is regenerated (checked: committed regen output).","id":"28d5-c980-ba43-4c6e","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"G7 contradicts_reality blocking at 0.85 plus abstain and dedup fixes"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384388513965001,"uuid":"d526e060-2b60-4dc3-a5b0-89799aacbaf0"}